  "answer": "Final sale does not prevent a warranty claim. A defective outlet tent follows the tent warranty assessment process, including proof of purchase and photos. Your separated stitching seam can qualify as a manufacturing defect under the 24-month tent warranty (you are within 18 months). Required evidence: proof of purchase and clear photos showing the failure. Cosmetic wear disclosed on the outlet listing is not a new defect, but your issue arose later and was not disclosed. An approved manufacturing-defect claim receives a prepaid ground label with no label fee deducted.",
  "abstain": false,
